{"step_index":87,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:55:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:55:25+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:55:25+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/guard.sh`\nTotal Lines: 53\nTotal Bytes: 1998\nShowing lines 1 to 53\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # guard.sh — protect the Lean layer and the verifier while agents run.\n3: #\n4: #   tools/antigravity/guard.sh lock   [PARTITION]   # prints REF_SHA for sbatch\n5: #   tools/antigravity/guard.sh unlock [PARTITION]\n6: #\n7: # `lock` hashes everything a false claim could be edited into agreement with —\n8: # the Lean definitions and their oleans, the verifier chain, the challenges —\n9: # makes those files read-only, and makes every directory under lean_project/.lake\n10: # read-only so that a stray `lake` cannot delete Mathlib.\n11: #\n12: # Read-only is only a guard against accidents: an agent running as this user can\n13: # chmod it back. The hashes are the real protection — the attempt job re-checks\n14: # them against a reference whose own digest arrives through the job environment.\n15: set -euo pipefail\n16: ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../..\" && pwd)\"\n17: PART=\"${2:-promising13}\"\n18: REF=\"$ROOT/handoff/$PART/.integrity.sha256\"\n19: LP=\"lean_project\"\n20: \n21: protected() {\n22:   ls $LP/LeanProject/*.lean \\\n23:      $LP/.lake/build/lib/lean/LeanProject.olean \\\n24:      $LP/.lake/build/lib/lean/LeanProject/*.olean \\\n25:      tools/antigravity_handoff.py tools/prover_eval/w16.py \\\n26:      pipeline/theorem_prover.py config.py tools/antigravity/check.sh \\\n27:      tools/antigravity/agy_home.sh tools/antigravity/sandbox.sh \\\n28:      handoff/.agf_lean_path handoff/.agf_env \\\n29:      benchmark/challenges_$PART/*.lean benchmark/challenges_$PART/index.json\n30: }\n31: \n32: cd \"$ROOT\"\n33: case \"${1:-}\" in\n34:   lock)\n35:     mkdir -p \"$(dirname \"$REF\")\"\n36:     [ -f \"$REF\" ] && chmod u+w \"$REF\"\n37:     protected | xargs sha256sum > \"$REF\"\n38:     protected | xargs chmod a-w\n39:     find \"$LP/.lake\" -type d -exec chmod a-w {} +\n40:     chmod a-w \"$REF\"\n41:     echo \"locked $(wc -l < \"$REF\") files; lean_project/.lake is read-only\"\n42:     echo \"REF_SHA=$(sha256sum \"$REF\" | cut -d' ' -f1)\"\n43:     ;;\n44:   unlock)\n45:     find \"$LP/.lake\" -type d -exec chmod u+w {} +\n46:     protected | xargs chmod u+w\n47:     [ -f \"$REF\" ] && chmod u+w \"$REF\"\n48:     echo \"unlocked\"\n49:     ;;\n50:   *)\n51:     echo \"usage: $0 lock|unlock [PARTITION]\"; exit 2 ;;\n52: esac\n53: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
