{"step_index":104,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:56:01Z","thinking":"**Applying cardinality bound theorem**\n\nThe `Finset.card_biUnion_le_card_mul` theorem directly applies to the problem. It relates the cardinality of a finite union to the cardinality of the index set and the bound on the cardinality of each set in the union. The hypothesis `h : ∀ a ∈ s, #(Sym2.toFinset a) ≤ n` is the crucial part that links the existing theorem to the specific expression of the problem, with `n` assigned to 2.\n\n\n**Connecting vertex count to edge cover**\n\nDetermining how `Fintype.card V ≤ 2 * k` relates to `edgeCoverNumber G` requires analyzing the definition of `edgeCoverNumber`. The definition leverages `minUpTo`, which has the form `(((range (n + 1)).filter p).min).getD n`. This filters a range and returns the minimum element that satisfies the predicate `p`, or `n` if no such element exists. The goal is to establish a connection between the bound on vertex cardinality and the edge cover number, which is the minimum size of an edge cover.\n\nA helper lemma is needed to gain further insight into `minUpTo`. The proposed lemma `minUpTo n p = n ∨ p (minUpTo n p)` can be checked to understand the behavior.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":false,"Includes":["*.lean"],"IsRegex":false,"MatchPerLine":true,"Query":"induction x using WithTop.recTopCoe","SearchPath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib","toolAction":"Searching for WithTop induction","toolSummary":"Grep WithTop induction"}}]}
