{"step_index":143,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:57:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:57:41+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:57:41+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Order/TypeTags.lean`\nTotal Lines: 74\nTotal Bytes: 1893\nShowing lines 1 to 30\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: /-\n2: Copyright (c) 2018 Mario Carneiro. All rights reserved.\n3: Released under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\n4: Authors: Mario Carneiro, Simon Hudon, Yury Kudryashov\n5: -/\n6: module\n7: \n8: public import Mathlib.Order.Notation\n9: \n10: /-!\n11: # Order-related type synonyms\n12: \n13: In this file we define `WithBot` and `WithTop`.\n14: -/\n15: \n16: @[expose] public section\n17: \n18: variable {α : Type*}\n19: \n20: /-- Attach `⊥` to a type. -/\n21: @[to_dual /-- Attach `⊤` to a type. -/]\n22: def WithBot (α : Type*) := Option α\n23: \n24: instance WithBot.instRepr [Repr α] : Repr (WithBot α) :=\n25:   ⟨fun o _ =>\n26:     match o with\n27:     | none => \"⊥\"\n28:     | some a => \"↑\" ++ repr a⟩\n29: \n30: @[to_dual existing]\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":144,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:57:41Z","thinking":"**Identifying Option Type Equivalence**\n\nThe type `WithBot` is equivalent to `Option α`, as is `WithTop`. The Lean `cases` statement structure for `Option α` can be directly applied. However, considering the context of the code, a different approach might be necessary.\n\n\n**Verifying Term Equivalence**\n\nThe `h` variable in the `cases` statement likely represents an equation. The equation should be of the form `s.min = some k`. The type of `Finset.mem_of_min` provides the key. `some k` and `↑k` are definitionally identical due to the definition of `WithTop`.\n\nTherefore, the equation `h : s.min = some k` matches the theorem's format. This is tested directly by modifying the lean file.\n\n\n**Evaluating Edge Cover Size**\n\nThe goal is to prove that the cardinality of the vertex set is less than or equal to twice the edge cover number. The definition of `GraphCalc.edgeCoverNumber` involves taking the minimum of the sizes of edge covers.  Using the provided lemma, the inequality can be established.\n\nIt's likely the case split in the `cases h` will either prove the statement, or require a separate proof. The next step is to examine the structure of the `some k` case.\n\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Implement prove_a23c41a0 in Challenge_a23c41a0.lean","EndLine":34,"Instruction":"Implement prove_a23c41a0","ReplacementContent":"theorem prove_a23c41a0 : Candidate := by\n  intro V _ _ G _ _ _\n  change Fintype.card V ≤ 2 * GraphCalc.edgeCoverNumber G\n  unfold GraphCalc.edgeCoverNumber GraphCalc.minUpTo\n  cases h : ((Finset.range (Fintype.card V + 1)).filter\n    (fun k => ∃ s ∈ G.edgeFinset.powersetCard k, GraphCalc.IsEdgeCoverFinset G s)).min with\n  | none =>\n    dsimp\n    omega\n  | some k =>\n    dsimp\n    have hk : k ∈ (Finset.range (Fintype.card V + 1)).filter\n      (fun k => ∃ s ∈ G.edgeFinset.powersetCard k, GraphCalc.IsEdgeCoverFinset G s) := Finset.mem_of_min h\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hk\n    rcases hk.2 with ⟨s, hs, hcov⟩\n    rw [Finset.mem_powersetCard] at hs\n    have hle := card_le_two_mul_card_of_isEdgeCoverFinset G s hcov\n    omega","StartLine":31,"TargetContent":"theorem prove_a23c41a0 : Candidate := by\n  sorry","TargetFile":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_a23c41a0/Challenge_a23c41a0.lean","toolAction":"Implementing prove_a23c41a0","toolSummary":"Implement prove_a23c41a0 in Challenge_a23c41a0.lean"}}]}
